    </div>
    <p class="mss-swipe">← Swipe for more →</p>
    <div class="mss-next"><a class="mss-btn" href="#shop">Meet five roasters · Shop</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mss-sec mss-sec--paper">
    <div class="mss-head">
      <p class="mss-eyebrow">Our Story</p>
      <h2 class="mss-h2">Heaven, earth and people in a name</h2>
      <p class="mss-sub">Sun, moon, mountain: three characters that paint a picture of heaven, earth and people.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mss-trio">
      <div><span class="mss-trio__k">天</span><h3 class="mss-h3">Heaven · Sun and moon</h3><p>The fullest light by day, the soft moon by night, and the stars farther still. Light comes from above; it makes all things grow and gives time its rhythm.</p></div>
      <div><span class="mss-trio__k">地</span><h3 class="mss-h3">Earth · The mountain</h3><p>The mountain never speaks, yet it holds everything. Coffee trees on its slopes take in the land and the light of sun and moon — that is where the taste of every bean begins.</p></div>
      <div><span class="mss-trio__k">人</span><h3 class="mss-h3">People · The roasters, and you</h3><p>Five roasters turn the land into flavour through fire. You, drinking this cup, are the final brushstroke of the painting.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="mss-spirit">
      <p class="mss-eyebrow">Brand Spirit</p>
      <p class="mss-quote">Still at heart as the mountain, radiant in celestial light.</p>
      <p>A mountain stands firm not because it escapes wind and rain, but because its roots run deep. Boil the water, wait, let the aroma rise, and sit down steady, like a mountain. The light of sun and moon falls on us, but we carry light of our own too — the warmth people feel around someone whose heart is settled and kind.</p>
      <p>Brewing yourself a cup every morning is a ritual, a taste, and a way of living.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mss-split mss-logo-meaning">
      <img src="https://mountsunmoon.com/assets/mark.png" alt="Mount Sun Moon symbol" loading="lazy" width="300" height="194">
      <div>
        <h3 class="mss-h3">The symbol in our logo</h3>
        <p><strong>Two peaks, climbing high to see far.</strong> The mountain line rises in two peaks, as if leading you onward. The gold of the mountain and the sun comes from the Loess Plateau; the moon is a clear, bright white.</p>
        <p><strong>Beyond what we see, endless possibility.</strong> The large gold circle is the sun; the smaller white circle in front is the moon. Offset, they form a golden crescent — what the eye sees is not always the whole picture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mss-sec">
    <div class="mss-head">
      <p class="mss-eyebrow">Origin Notes</p>
      <h2 class="mss-h2">Which mountain does your cup come from?</h2>
      <p class="mss-sub">The five roasters' beans come from high mountains in six countries on three continents.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="mss-wide" src="{{ img_farm }}&width=1600" alt="A highland coffee farm in the morning mist" loading="lazy" width="1536" height="1024">
    <div class="mss-origins">
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Kenya · Kirinyaga</h3><p class="mss-meta">approx. 1,600–1,900 m | Emily</p><p>Red volcanic soil on the southern slopes of Mount Kenya gives bright acidity; washed Kenyans often show blackcurrant and berry. AA is the top screen grade.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Indonesia · Sumatra</h3><p class="mss-meta">Mandheling | Warren · Fetod</p><p>Wet-hulling brings a heavy body with cocoa and herbal notes; Fetod's natural-process Solok Mandheling is sweeter and more aromatic.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Guatemala · Huehuetenango</h3><p class="mss-meta">approx. 1,500–2,000 m | Warren · Kason & Chuck</p><p>Northwestern highlands where warm dry winds keep frost away; clean cups with full sweetness.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Ethiopia · Yirgacheffe</h3><p class="mss-meta">approx. 1,700–2,200 m | Warren</p><p>The birthplace of Arabica, famous for florals and citrus; natural processing adds ripe-fruit sweetness.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Colombia · Supremo</h3><p class="mss-meta">Andes | Warren</p><p>Supremo is a size grade (screen 17 and up); balanced flavour, round sweetness.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="mss-h4">Honduras</h3><p class="mss-meta">approx. 1,400–1,550 m | Dahe · Elias</p><p>A fast-rising specialty origin where small farms experiment with honey and anaerobic processing.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="mss-swipe">← Swipe for more →</p>
    <p class="mss-note">Altitudes are typical ranges for each region and vary by lot and farm.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mss-sec mss-sec--paper" id="brew">
    <div class="mss-head">
      <p class="mss-eyebrow">How to Brew</p>
      <h2 class="mss-h2">A slow morning cup in five steps</h2>
      <p class="mss-sub">Water at 88–92°C, 150–180 ml per bag.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="mss-fig">
      <img class="mss-wide" src="{{ 'mss-senbei.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Rice crackers stamped with the Mount Sun Moon symbol beside a cup of coffee in morning light" loading="lazy" width="1264" height="848">
      <figcaption>A rice cracker with your coffee, and a slow morning. The Collector's Gift Box includes limited Kobayashi rice crackers (styled image).</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="mss-steps">
      <li><span>1</span>Tap the bag so the grounds settle, then tear along the dotted line.</li>
      <li><span>2</span>Open the side hooks and hang the filter on your cup.</li>
      <li><span>3</span>Pour a little hot water and let it bloom for 20 seconds.</li>
      <li><span>4</span>Pour in stages up to 150–180 ml.</li>
      <li><span>5</span>Lift out the filter, let it drain, and enjoy.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="mss-next"><a class="mss-btn" href="#shop">Pick a cup, start tomorrow morning!</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mss-sec" id="faq">
    <div class="mss-head">
      <p class="mss-eyebrow">Ordering & FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="mss-h2">Ordering information</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mss-faq">
      <details open><summary>What is Mount Sun Moon?</summary><p>Mount Sun Moon (日月山) is a Taiwanese specialty drip-bag coffee brand by Fetod Ltd. Every box holds signature beans from five independent roasters, from Kenya, Indonesia, Guatemala, Ethiopia, Colombia and Honduras, so you can compare five flavours at home with nothing but hot water.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you ship outside Taiwan?</summary><p>Online orders currently ship within Taiwan. For overseas orders or corporate gifts, please contact us on LINE or at hello@mountsunmoon.com.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Shipping time and cost</summary><p>Orders ship in order from 1 December. Orders paid by 18 December should arrive before Christmas. Free shipping on orders over NT$1,000; otherwise NT$85 within Taiwan.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do I pay?</summary><p>Bank transfer for now: the account details appear on the order confirmation page and email. Please transfer within 3 days and report your order number and the last five digits of your account on the <a href="/pages/remit">payment report page</a>. Card payment is coming soon.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you make corporate or custom gift boxes?</summary><p>Yes. Orders of 100 sets or more receive corporate pricing, and we can print your logo on the box or card — ideal for year-end parties, Lunar New Year, staff benefits, client thank-yous and trade shows. Contact us on LINE or by email for a quote.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How many cups does one bag make?</summary><p>Each bag holds 10 g ± 1 g of ground coffee for one 150–180 ml cup.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How long does the coffee keep?</summary><p>12 months unopened at room temperature. Keep it cool and dry, away from sunlight, and brew soon after opening.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

